# `@ts-expect-error` ban

`src/` must stay at **zero** `@ts-expect-error` / `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-nocheck`.
ESLint `@typescript-eslint/ban-ts-comment` enforces this.

## Required workflow when types fail

1. Prefer **real types**: generics (`useState<T>`, `useRef<T | null>`), interfaces, type guards.
2. Third-party gaps: add or extend a module in `src/types/*.d.ts`, or a **narrow** cast at the import/call boundary (`as SpecificType`).
3. Do **not** add `@ts-expect-error`, `@ts-ignore`, or `@ts-nocheck`.
4. Do **not** run bulk `ts-migrate reignore` — it injects comments into JSX as text nodes.

```text
❌ BAD — // @ts-expect-error vendor missing prop
❌ BAD — // @ts-ignore
✅ GOOD — declare module / src/types/*.d.ts augmentation
✅ GOOD — const Editor = MdEditor as ComponentType<OurProps>
✅ GOOD — useState<ChatMessage[]>([])
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
